---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Area Activities & Amenities | The Bluffs — Overlooking Weiss Lake"
  description="The Bluffs offers miles of trails, community gardens, private lake access, and proximity to Little River Canyon, DeSoto State Park, and 30,000 acres of Weiss Lake."
  image="/assets/images/pages/activities-dock.jpg"
>

  <!-- HERO -->
  <div class="page-hero">
    <img
      src="/assets/images/pages/activities-dock.jpg"
      alt="Private gated lake access with dock and picnic area at The Bluffs"
      width="1920"
      height="800"
      fetchpriority="high"
    />
    <div class="page-hero-overlay">
      <h1 class="page-hero-title">Activities &amp; Amenities at The Bluffs</h1>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- INTRO -->
  <section class="section intro-section">
    <div class="container-narrow text-center">
      <h2>Return to Nature</h2>
      <p class="intro-text">
        The Bluffs was designed around a simple philosophy: the land itself is the amenity.
        Rather than building expensive clubhouses and infrastructure upfront and charging
        residents for them through high HOA dues, The Bluffs keeps dues low and lets the
        community grow its shared amenities organically over time. What you get from day one
        is direct access to some of the finest natural surroundings in the Southeast.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3-COLUMN FEATURE GRID -->
  <section class="section-sm features-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="features-grid">

        <article class="feature-card">
          <div class="feature-img">
            <img
              src="/assets/images/pages/activities-trails.jpg"
              alt="Walking and biking trails through the forested mountain terrain at The Bluffs"
              width="600"
              height="400"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </div>
          <div class="feature-body">
            <h3>Trails</h3>
            <p>
              Almost a dozen miles of walking, biking, horseback, and 4-wheeler trails wind
              through The Bluffs' mountain terrain. The trail network connects homesites to
              overlooks, the lake, and quiet forest clearings — built for everyday use, not
              just special occasions.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="feature-card">
          <div class="feature-img">
            <img
              src="/assets/images/pages/activities-gardens.jpg"
              alt="Community gardens and restored orchard at The Bluffs"
              width="600"
              height="400"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </div>
          <div class="feature-body">
            <h3>Community Gardens</h3>
            <p>
              The community gardens and restored orchard — with 28 fruit and nut varieties —
              are shared spaces for growing produce, gathering with neighbors, and enjoying
              a slower pace. Spring-fed irrigation keeps the orchard productive through
              Alabama's warm seasons.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="feature-card">
          <div class="feature-img">
            <img
              src="/assets/images/pages/activities-dock.jpg"
              alt="Private gated access to Weiss Lake with dock and picnic area"
              width="600"
              height="400"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </div>
          <div class="feature-body">
            <h3>Lake Access</h3>
            <p>
              Private, gated access to Weiss Lake — with covered docks, picnic grounds, and
              shoreline areas exclusively for community residents and guests. A quiet spot
              to launch a kayak, fish from the dock, or simply sit and watch the water.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="divider" style="max-width: var(--max-width); margin: 0 auto;" />

  <!-- REGIONAL ATTRACTIONS -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="region-header text-center">
        <h2>The Surrounding Region</h2>
        <p class="region-intro">
          The Bluffs sits at the center of one of the most scenically rich corners of the
          Southeast — with world-class outdoor recreation, history, and natural wonders all
          within an easy drive.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="region-grid">

        <div class="region-item">
          <h3>Weiss Lake</h3>
          <p>
            30,000 acres, 52 miles long, and known worldwide as the crappie fishing capital
            of the world. Three river tributaries — the Coosa, Little River, and Chattooga —
            feed the lake, creating diverse habitat for bass, crappie, catfish, and more.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="region-item">
          <h3>Little River Canyon</h3>
          <p>
            One of the deepest river gorges east of the Mississippi, Little River Canyon
            National Preserve offers hiking, waterfalls, rock climbing, and kayaking less
            than 25 miles from The Bluffs.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="region-item">
          <h3>DeSoto State Park</h3>
          <p>
            Adjacent to Little River Canyon, DeSoto State Park offers cabins, camping,
            a swimming pool, and miles of scenic trails through rhododendron-lined gorges
            and forested ridge tops.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="region-item">
          <h3>Piedmont Mountain Range</h3>
          <p>
            The rolling ridgelines of the Piedmont Mountain Range form a constant backdrop —
            visible from most homesites at The Bluffs, especially on clear fall and winter days
            when the hardwoods drop their leaves and the views open up for miles.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="region-item">
          <h3>Cherokee &amp; Civil War History</h3>
          <p>
            Cherokee County is rich in Native American and Civil War history, with museums
            in Centre, historic sites throughout the county, and the legacy of the Cherokee
            Nation's presence in this part of Alabama and Georgia.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="region-item">
          <h3>Golf &amp; Recreation</h3>
          <p>
            Multiple golf courses, the Chattokee Lodge, state parks, and a variety of local
            marinas and boat ramps make the area a year-round recreation destination for
            both residents and visitors.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="section-sm cta-band">
    <div class="container text-center">
      <p>Come see it for yourself.</p>
      <div class="cta-buttons">
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Schedule a Visit</a>
        <a href="/homesites" class="btn btn-outline">View Available Homesites</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* Intro */
  .intro-section {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-olive-light);
  }

  .intro-section h2 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .intro-text {
    font-size: var(--text-md);
    color: var(--color-charcoal-mid);
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* Feature cards */
  .features-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-8);
  }

  .feature-card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-olive-light);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .feature-img img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 240px;
    object-fit: cover;
    display: block;
  }

  .feature-body {
    padding: var(--space-6);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .feature-body h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .feature-body p {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-charcoal-mid);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* Regional attractions */
  .region-header {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-10);
  }

  .region-header h2 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .region-intro {
    font-size: var(--text-md);
    color: var(--color-charcoal-mid);
    max-width: 680px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .region-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-8);
  }

  .region-item {
    padding: var(--space-5) 0;
    border-top: 2px solid var(--color-olive-light);
  }

  .region-item h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
    color: var(--color-teal);
  }

  .region-item p {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-charcoal-mid);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* CTA band */
  .cta-band {
    background: var(--color-cream-dark);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-olive-light);
  }

  .cta-band p {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }

  .cta-buttons {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    justify-content: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .features-grid,
    .region-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .features-grid,
    .region-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
